  "notes": "Follows the portal orchestration (pco2_tool.R): both replicate slots always run through calcCH4dry -> calcCO2 -> calcpCO2/P1/P2 -> calcCH4, so a single-replicate full_pipeline run emits the _A keys alongside the _avg keys, where the Rust impl emitted only _avg (full_single_replicate, lab_conditions_from_constants). d13C avg/sd come from calcMean/calcSd over the A/B pair (na.rm), so a one-sided d13C yields the lone value as avg with sd absent, matching the Rust pco2 behavior. Simple mode with a missing co2_aq_umol returns the key absent (portal NA) where the Rust impl returned 400; simple-mode P1/P2 pass pressure_hpa through the portal Field_BP band check (700-1050 hPa, fallback altitude NA), so an out-of-band pressure omits the key rather than computing with it. An entered lab_pressure_hpa outside 700-1050 hPa raises an error, mirroring the Rust guard against atm-style entries. vol_sa_ml/vol_water_ml request overrides are substituted into the constants frame because the portal calcCO2 reads volumes from the constants table only. Gas constants used: c_const, gas_const_r_atm, gas_const_r_mol, h_ch4_29815k, ch4_in_sa; lab fallbacks: lab_temp_avg_degC, lab_press_avg_atm (atm, applied without conversion), vol_sa, vol_water. calcCH4 uses the portal's 0.957237 atm literal, not the entered lab pressure. No curves."
}